//
// These annotations carry only Redis concepts: Pub/Sub channels (plain,
// pattern and sharded), Streams with consumer groups and trimming, Lists
// used as queues, keyspace notifications, and Redis specifics of servers and
// authentication. Everything generic (info, servers, security schemes, tags,
// summaries, examples, headers, ...) uses the asyncapi.v3 annotations
// (asyncapi/v3/annotations.proto).
//
// A service only needs enough annotations to say "this is a Redis API";
// everything else is inferred from the Protobuf schema and its comments:
//
//   - request/reply vs. publish vs. subscribe is inferred from the rpc shape,
//     as documented on Pattern;
//   - channel names and keys default to
//     "<package>:<service>:<method>", with ':' separators in snake_case;
//   - `{name}` placeholders in channel names and keys are AsyncAPI channel
//     parameters, bound to payload fields with the same name. Subscribers of
//     parameterized Pub/Sub channels use pattern subscriptions (PSUBSCRIBE).
//     In Redis Cluster, a placeholder that is the key's hash tag is written
